From 09b44f71877b80bbd861d52e63fd69695bc8eeec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vividh Yadav <178728541+VividhDesign@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:07:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Searches no longer block while a batch is inserted

add() now holds the index lock exclusively only for a short first phase
(allocate nodes, store vectors, update the label map) and links the new nodes
under the shared lock. While an insert is linking, queries copy neighbour
lists under the per-node spinlocks; otherwise they keep the lock-free path.
Writers are serialised by a separate mutex.

Collection::upsert no longer holds the collection lock across the WAL write
and the index insert: metadata is updated under a short exclusive lock and the
vectors are indexed while queries continue.

bench/bench_ingest: inserting 100k vectors into a 100k index (18 s), the old
code answered 2 queries (one waited 18.4 s); now 80k queries are answered
with p50 0.20 ms / p99 0.43 ms. Insert time is unchanged. TSan and ASan clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PHDAJht8Mhyh4r51AFKp8J
